[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: Fencing Vision - Core Product Requirements
UID: FV-CORE

[GRAMMAR]
IMPORT_FROM_FILE: @fencing-vision-requirement

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-AUTH-001
STATUS: Draft
SOURCE: CAP-ACCESS
VERIFICATION: Automated test
TITLE: Authentication required
STATEMENT: The system shall require an authenticated user for every clip upload, processing, library, export, and sharing operation.

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-AUTH-002
STATUS: Draft
SOURCE: CAP-ACCESS
VERIFICATION: Automated test
TITLE: Passwordless sign-in
STATEMENT: The system shall allow a user to sign in using a magic link or a supported identity provider without creating a password.

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-AUTH-003
STATUS: Draft
SOURCE: CAP-ACCESS
VERIFICATION: Automated test
TITLE: No guest accounts
STATEMENT: The system shall not create anonymous or guest accounts or accept guest uploads.

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-AUTH-004
STATUS: Draft
SOURCE: CAP-ACCESS
VERIFICATION: Automated test
TITLE: Session management
STATEMENT: The system shall allow an authenticated user to inspect and terminate their active session.

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-AUTH-005
STATUS: Draft
SOURCE: CAP-ACCESS
VERIFICATION: Automated test
TITLE: Fencing context
STATEMENT: The system shall record the user's weapon hand, stance, and direction of travel independently so pose keypoints can be described using fencing-relative terminology.

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-CLIP-001
STATUS: Draft
SOURCE: CAP-CLIPS
VERIFICATION: Automated test
TITLE: Recording guidance
STATEMENT: The system shall present recording guidance describing the framing and recording conditions required for a supported clip.

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-CLIP-002
STATUS: Draft
SOURCE: CAP-CLIPS
VERIFICATION: Automated test
TITLE: Clip upload context
STATEMENT: The system shall allow an authenticated user to upload a clip with an action type, weapon hand, camera view, and optional notes.

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-CLIP-003
STATUS: Draft
SOURCE: CAP-CLIPS
VERIFICATION: Automated test
TITLE: Action selection
STATEMENT: The system shall allow a user to select or trim the portion of an uploaded clip that contains the action to be analysed.

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-CLIP-004
STATUS: Draft
SOURCE: CAP-CLIPS
VERIFICATION: Automated test
TITLE: Upload validation
STATEMENT: The system shall reject clips that exceed supported file-size or duration limits or that do not contain a supported detected media type.

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-CLIP-005
STATUS: Draft
SOURCE: CAP-CLIPS
VERIFICATION: Automated test
TITLE: Upload rejection guidance
STATEMENT: When a clip is rejected, the system shall explain the violated constraint in language suitable for the user.

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-CLIP-006
STATUS: Draft
SOURCE: CAP-CLIPS
VERIFICATION: Automated test
TITLE: Private source storage
STATEMENT: The system shall store original uploaded clips as private assets owned by the uploading user.

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-CLIP-007
STATUS: Draft
SOURCE: CAP-CLIPS
VERIFICATION: Automated test
TITLE: Processing state visibility
STATEMENT: The system shall show whether a clip is uploading, queued, processing, completed, unsuitable for analysis, or failed.

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-CLIP-008
STATUS: Draft
SOURCE: CAP-CLIPS
VERIFICATION: Automated test
TITLE: Private clip library
STATEMENT: The system shall provide each authenticated user with a private library showing their clips, upload dates, thumbnails, processing states, and available analysis versions.

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-CLIP-009
STATUS: Draft
SOURCE: CAP-CLIPS
VERIFICATION: Automated test
TITLE: Clip details
STATEMENT: The system shall provide an owner with a clip detail view containing the clip video, metadata, analyses, and sharing state.

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-CLIP-010
STATUS: Draft
SOURCE: CAP-CLIPS
VERIFICATION: Automated test
TITLE: Editable clip metadata
STATEMENT: The system shall allow an owner to edit a clip's title and notes without uploading the media again.

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-CLIP-011
STATUS: Draft
SOURCE: CAP-CLIPS
VERIFICATION: Automated test
TITLE: Clip deletion
STATEMENT: The system shall allow an owner to permanently delete a clip and all associated derived assets, analyses, exports, and share links.

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-MEDIA-001
STATUS: Draft
SOURCE: CAP-TRUST
VERIFICATION: Automated test
TITLE: Original media preservation
STATEMENT: The system shall preserve the original uploaded video separately from transcoded or annotated derivatives.

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-MEDIA-002
STATUS: Draft
SOURCE: CAP-TRUST
VERIFICATION: Automated test
TITLE: Original checksum
STATEMENT: The system shall calculate the source clip checksum from the original uploaded bytes rather than from a derivative or model output.

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-MEDIA-003
STATUS: Draft
SOURCE: CAP-TRUST
VERIFICATION: Automated test
TITLE: Distinct asset records
STATEMENT: The system shall represent original media, analysis inputs, annotated media, thumbnails, raw detections, derived results, and exports as distinct assets.

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-MEDIA-004
STATUS: Draft
SOURCE: CAP-TRUST
VERIFICATION: Automated test
TITLE: Asset metadata
STATEMENT: The system shall record the owner, source clip, creation time, content type, byte size, checksum, and retention state of every stored asset.

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-MEDIA-005
STATUS: Draft
SOURCE: CAP-TRUST
VERIFICATION: Automated test
TITLE: Visible retention
STATEMENT: The system shall make applicable asset-retention periods visible to the user before automatic expiry can remove an asset.

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-MEDIA-006
STATUS: Draft
SOURCE: CAP-TRUST
VERIFICATION: Automated test
TITLE: Source media metadata
STATEMENT: The system shall record the source video's dimensions, duration, frame timing, orientation, and any transcoding applied for analysis.
